&lt;aside class=&quot;dk-callout dk-callout--aside&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dk-callout__body&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;An aside holds a tangential remark.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;callouts-carrying-attributes&quot;&gt;Callouts carrying attributes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Starlight-mapped class that carries a &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{#id}&lt;/code&gt; or a &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{icon:}&lt;/code&gt; routes through the
&lt;strong&gt;theme&lt;/strong&gt; callout instead of the native aside, because the native aside path
discards attributes. The class becomes the fallback variant (for a tip,
&lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;dk-callout--tip&lt;/code&gt;) so the id and icon survive on the &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;#x3C;aside&gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;aside class=&quot;dk-callout dk-callout--tip&quot; id=&quot;pinned-tip&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dk-callout__body&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This tip carries an id, so it rides the theme callout and keeps &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;id=&quot;pinned-tip&quot;&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;
&lt;aside class=&quot;dk-callout dk-callout--tip&quot; id=&quot;icon-tip&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;dk-callout__icon&quot; data-icon=&quot;rocket&quot;&gt;&lt;svg class=&quot;dk-callout__icon-glyph&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 24 24&quot; fill=&quot;currentColor&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&quot;evenodd&quot; d=&quot;M1.44 8.855v-.001l3.527-3.516c.34-.344.802-.541 1.285-.548h6.649l.947-.947c3.07-3.07 6.207-3.072 7.62-2.868a1.821 1.821 0 0 1 1.557 1.557c.204 1.413.203 4.55-2.868 7.62l-.946.946v6.649a1.845 1.845 0 0 1-.549 1.286l-3.516 3.528a1.844 1.844 0 0 1-3.11-.944l-.858-4.275-4.52-4.52-2.31-.463-1.964-.394A1.847 1.847 0 0 1 .98 10.693a1.843 1.843 0 0 1 .46-1.838Zm5.379 2.017-3.873-.776L6.32 6.733h4.638l-4.14 4.14Zm8.403-5.655c2.459-2.46 4.856-2.463 5.89-2.33.134 1.035.13 3.432-2.329 5.891l-6.71 6.71-3.561-3.56 6.71-6.711Zm-1.318 15.837-.776-3.873 4.14-4.14v4.639l-3.364 3.374Z&quot; clip-rule=&quot;evenodd&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M9.318 18.345a.972.972 0 0 0-1.86-.561c-.482 1.435-1.687 2.204-2.934 2.619a8.22 8.22 0 0 1-1.23.302c.062-.365.157-.79.303-1.229.415-1.247 1.184-2.452 2.62-2.935a.971.971 0 1 0-.62-1.842c-.12.04-.236.084-.35.13-2.02.828-3.012 2.588-3.493 4.033a10.383 10.383 0 0 0-.51 2.845l-.001.016v.063c0 .536.434.972.97.972H2.24a7.21 7.21 0 0 0 .878-.065c.527-.063 1.248-.19 2.02-.447 1.445-.48 3.205-1.472 4.033-3.494a5.828 5.828 0 0 0 .147-.407Z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dk-callout__body&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This tip carries a &lt;strong&gt;mapped&lt;/strong&gt; icon (&lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;fa-lightbulb&lt;/code&gt;), which resolves and renders. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;figures&quot;&gt;Figures&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An image with a &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{…}&lt;/code&gt; attribute list above it becomes an accessible &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;#x3C;figure&gt;&lt;/code&gt;:
the bracket text is the caption, &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{alt:}&lt;/code&gt; is the alt text, and sizing/alignment/
class/id attributes are honoured.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure class=&quot;dk-figure dk-figure--center featured&quot; id=&quot;palm-fig&quot;&gt;a palm-lined tropical beach&lt;figcaption class=&quot;dk-figure__caption&quot;&gt;Palm Trees&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A web image passes through unoptimised, and &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{caption:}&lt;/code&gt; overrides the bracket
text while &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{height:}&lt;/code&gt; sizes it. The web URL here is this site’s own copy of the
image (served from &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;example/public/&lt;/code&gt;), so the page loads no image from another
host:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure class=&quot;dk-figure dk-figure--left&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://spec-kitty.github.io/doc-kitty/macintosh.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; style=&quot;height: 240&quot;&gt;&lt;figcaption class=&quot;dk-figure__caption&quot;&gt;The original Macintosh&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An unsupported attribute such as &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{fullbleed:}&lt;/code&gt; is silently ignored — no error,
the figure still renders:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure class=&quot;dk-figure&quot;&gt;a lighthouse at dusk&lt;figcaption class=&quot;dk-figure__caption&quot;&gt;Lighthouse&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;crosslink-ids&quot;&gt;Crosslink ids&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Put &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{#id}&lt;/code&gt; above a heading to give it a stable anchor, then link to it. Explicit
ids win over the auto-generated slug, and headings with no Markua keep their slug.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;intro&quot;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This section has an explicit &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{#intro}&lt;/code&gt; anchor. Jump to the
&lt;a href=&quot;#intro&quot;&gt;introduction&lt;/a&gt; or straight to the &lt;a href=&quot;#overview&quot;&gt;overview&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;overview&quot;&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This heading’s text would auto-slug to &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;overview&lt;/code&gt; too; the explicit &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{#overview}&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;wins&lt;/strong&gt; and no duplicate anchor is produced. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;plain-heading-automatic-anchor&quot;&gt;Plain heading, automatic anchor&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This heading carries no Markua syntax, so it keeps its automatic
&lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;plain-heading-automatic-anchor&lt;/code&gt; slug (FR-008). &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;span-ids&quot;&gt;Span ids&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can anchor an inline span. The bracketed form wraps its label:
&lt;span id=&quot;beach-span&quot;&gt;the beach&lt;/span&gt; — and the trailing form wraps the preceding word:
&lt;span id=&quot;shoreline-span&quot;&gt;shoreline&lt;/span&gt;. Jump to the &lt;a href=&quot;#beach-span&quot;&gt;beach span&lt;/a&gt; or the
&lt;a href=&quot;#shoreline-span&quot;&gt;shoreline span&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;an-attribute-above-a-wrapper&quot;&gt;An attribute above a wrapper&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An id placed immediately above an &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{aside}&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;{blurb}&lt;/code&gt;) wrapper lands on the
container itself:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;aside class=&quot;dk-callout dk-callout--aside&quot; id=&quot;anchored-aside&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;dk-callout__body&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This aside carries &lt;code dir=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;id=&quot;anchored-aside&quot;&lt;/code&gt; from the attribute line above it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;
